{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And every shrub of the field.</b> It should have said 'and every tree of the field,' but it said שיח from the root of לשוח בשדה, which our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted as meaning prayer, and it comes to allude that all the trees and plants praise and extol the Holy One, blessed be He, in the manner that our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded on the verse (Psalms 65:14) ״יתרועעו אף ישירו״ — that the grain stalks sing song, and their song is their praise — for the Holy One, blessed be He, desired that His praise ascend from every species, even from the possessors of the vegetative soul."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:09:12.067646439Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}